---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageBanner from '../../components/PageBanner.astro';

const title = 'Terms of Service — Sanshi Bio';
const description = 'Terms for Sanshi Bio pigeon testing services: orders, samples, reports, re-tests, payment, data, intellectual property and liability.';
const breadcrumbLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://sanshibio.net/en/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Terms of Service' },
  ],
};
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} jsonLd={[breadcrumbLd]}>
  <PageBanner title="Terms of Service" description="Please read the service scope, sample requirements and report limits before ordering" breadcrumb="Terms of Service" />

  <section class="container-site py-16">
    <div class="prose-sanshi mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-500"><em>Last updated: 2026-11-24</em></p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold">1. Scope</h2>
      <p>
        These terms apply to testing services provided by Hebei Sanshi Biotechnology Co., Ltd.
        (“Sanshi Bio”): racing-pigeon gene testing, pathogen testing, paternity testing, sex
        identification and related technical services. The project scope, sample requirements, price,
        turnaround and report format are set by the quotation, order or written agreement confirmed by
        both parties. If there is a conflict, the specific order terms prevail.
      </p>
      <p>
        Testing is a laboratory service and an interpretation of a sample. It is <b>not a veterinary
        diagnosis, a treatment, or a prediction of race performance</b>. A report does not replace a
        veterinarian's clinical judgement and does not guarantee racing results, breeding outcomes or
        transaction value.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold">2. Client and samples</h2>
      <p>
        The client must provide accurate bird ID, ring number, contact details, sample origin and test
        purpose, and must be entitled to submit the sample. Samples must be collected, labelled,
        stored and shipped according to Sanshi Bio's instructions. We may reject a sample or request
        re-sampling where the sample is insufficient, degraded, contaminated, mislabelled or
        improperly stored or transported.
      </p>
      <p>
        The client must not submit samples of unknown or unlawful origin, or samples that create an
        undisclosed laboratory safety risk. The client must disclose known infectious or biosafety
        risks and comply with applicable law and carrier requirements.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold">3. Testing, reports and interpretation</h2>
      <p>
        We test according to the confirmed project and laboratory procedures. A report reflects the
        result <span style="font-weight:600">for the received sample under the testing conditions
        used</span>. Results can be affected by sampling time, site, sample quality, pathogen load,
        individual variation and method limits. A negative result does not necessarily exclude
        infection; a positive result does not necessarily mean clinical disease. Interpret results
        with clinical signs, epidemiology, re-testing and veterinary advice.
      </p>
      <p>
        The client should read the sample ID, test scope, reference range and limitations in the
        report. Questions should be raised promptly after receipt. Re-testing follows the agreed
        re-test plan and fees.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold">4. Price, payment and delivery</h2>
      <p>
        Test fees, sample handling, re-test fees, rush charges, shipping and taxes are set by the
        quotation or order. Unless agreed otherwise, payment is due before testing begins. Reports are
        normally delivered electronically; paper or other formats must be agreed in advance. Turnaround
        is an estimate and may change because of sample quality, re-testing, holidays, logistics or
        force majeure.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold">5. Cancellation, re-testing and refunds</h2>
      <p>
        Cancellation before testing begins is handled under the order terms. If a sample has been
        received, processed or testing has begun, costs already incurred may apply. If a failure is
        caused by the laboratory, we will arrange a re-test or refund as agreed in the order. Failures
        caused by sample quality, incorrect information, client action or force majeure are not a
        laboratory breach. Specific re-test, refund and liability arrangements are governed by the
        written order and applicable law.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold">6. Report use and intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        Reports are for the client or a written authorised recipient, for lawful breeding, health
        management, transaction verification or registration. The client must not forge, alter,
        misquote or use a report to mislead a counterparty, invent a pedigree, impersonate a testing
        body or infringe another person's rights.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our report templates, methods, databases, text and marks are protected by law. They may not be
        copied, adapted, published or used for commercial training without written permission. The
        client may keep and use the original report for their own birds.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold">7. Data and samples</h2>
      <p>
        Personal information is handled under our <a href="/en/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.
        Sample and test-data retention, destruction, and the use of third-party laboratories or service
        providers follow the project, order and applicable law. You may contact us to request deletion
        of personal information or samples, except where law or quality-record requirements require
        retention.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold">8. Limits of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the extent permitted by law, Sanshi Bio is not liable for indirect loss, lost profit, lost
        race results or loss caused by the client's use or misuse of a report, sample problems, the
        bird's condition, training, transaction decisions or third-party conduct. For a specific
        testing service we provide, our liability is limited to the testing fee actually received for
        that order, except where mandatory law prohibits that limitation.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold">9. Force majeure and changes</h2>
      <p>
        We will notify the client and discuss alternatives where a natural disaster, epidemic,
        government action, logistics interruption, equipment failure or other event beyond reasonable
        control causes delay or prevents performance. We may update these terms; the updated version
        will be published on this page, and a specific order is governed by the version confirmed when
        the order was placed.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold">10. Governing law and contact</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of the People's Republic of China. Disputes should first
        be addressed by discussion; if unresolved, they are submitted to the competent court at Sanshi
        Bio's place of operation. For questions about these terms, orders, samples or reports, use the
        <a href="/en/contact">contact page</a> or email
        <a href="mailto:martin@senobiocorp.com">martin@senobiocorp.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
